course: dictionary
lesson: 7514
title: Pour: liquids, rain and crowds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word pour has more than one meaning, so the clues in the sentence tell you which one to use. The most common meaning is to make a liquid flow out of a container. «Pour the milk into the jug slowly, so it does not spill.» The word milk is a clue: a liquid is moving out of a container.
explain: Look at what is doing the pouring. When rain pours, it falls very hard. «It's pouring, so grab your coat!» Nobody is holding a jug here, so pour means the rain is falling heavily.
explain: Pour can also mean lots of people or things moving fast together. «Crowds poured out of the stadium when the match ended.» Crowds are not liquids, but they move so many and so quickly that they flow like water. Ask yourself: what is moving, and is it a liquid, rain, or a crowd?
fact: Pour means to make a liquid flow out of a container.
fact: «Pouring» can describe heavy rain: «It's pouring».
fact: Pour (in, out) can mean lots of people or things move fast, as in «letters poured in».
fact: «Wax crayons are made of melted coloured wax poured into moulds.» Here pour is about liquid wax filling a mould.
fact: The forms are pour, pours, poured and pouring: «Ali poured the juice yesterday.»
exercise: «Ali poured the juice into a tall glass.» What does pour mean here? | To run away fast | *To make a liquid flow out of a container | To fall from the sky very hard | To shut tightly
exercise: «It's pouring, so grab your coat!» What is falling? | Milk | *Rain | Sand | Letters
exercise: «Crowds poured out of the stadium.» What does poured suggest? | A quiet walk by one person | *Lots of people moving fast together, flowing out | A liquid in a jug | Someone sleeping inside
test: «Many rivers pour fresh water into the Baltic Sea.» What does pour mean here? | To freeze solid | *To flow in, like a liquid moving into a container | To dry up slowly | To fall very hard from the sky
test: «Most trees die if you pour salty sea water on their roots.» What is being poured? | *Salty sea water | Sand from the beach | Feathers | Sunshine
exam: «Letters poured in all week after the news spread.» What does poured in mean? | Fell hard from the sky | Dried slowly | *Arrived in large numbers, quickly | Melted into moulds
